peacemachine-dvd-ripper (1.0.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Window controls are drawn as the house discs - round, black face, green
    ring - instead of GTK's default pills, so the app matches C0D3D's desktop
    on machines that have no hyprbars plugin.

 -- William James Sova (C0D3D) <william@peacemachinestudios.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:48:00 -0500

peacemachine-dvd-ripper (1.0.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the Matrix skin on machines that are not C0D3D's: the rain tiles were
    referenced by absolute home-directory paths, so the animated binary and the
    card rain drew nothing. The tiles now ship with the package and the app
    resolves them at runtime.
  * Add python3-cairo as a dependency — it draws the orbiting folder spinner
    and the blue binary behind it, and was missing, which is why the spinner
    was invisible on a fresh install.

 -- William James Sova (C0D3D) <william@peacemachinestudios.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:40:00 -0500

peacemachine-dvd-ripper (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Window buttons: the headerbar's clearance for the Hyprland hyprbars discs
    is now applied only under Hyprland. On other desktops the app shows its own
    minimise/maximise/close buttons at the window edge instead of leaving a gap.

 -- William James Sova (C0D3D) <william@peacemachinestudios.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:36:00 -0500

peacemachine-dvd-ripper (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: DVD and video-file ripping with per-episode naming,
    chapter and timestamp splits, lossless copy split, and three skins.

